1
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:05,780
Ah, done with another
grueling day of school.

2
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:08,591
Now all I want to do is go home and relax.

3
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:10,960
Huh? Huh?

4
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:14,180
Uh, Koichi, it's… you.

5
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:16,380
Hey there, Hazamada.

6
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:18,600
Oh, yeah, hi, what's new?

7
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:22,293
I'm sorry about all the trouble
I gave you the other day.

8
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:26,213
So, uh, have you completely
recovered from your injuries?

9
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:27,620
Sort of, I guess.

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,059
The talk sent me home two days ago.

11
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:32,835
Where's that bastard?

12
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:34,413
I mean, where's Josuke?

13
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:36,440
He probably already went home.

14
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:39,677
You won't believe it, but he
found an invisible baby yesterday.

15
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:42,717
And now they're bending over
backwards to find its mother.

16
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,780
So the baby is a stand user?

17
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:45,882
Looks that way.

18
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:49,997
Apparently, the baby has formed
a bond with Josuke's dad, Mr.

19
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:50,910
Joestar.

20
00:00:50,993 --> 00:00:51,900
In fact, if Mr.

21
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,217
Joestar isn't nearby at all times, she
turns everything around her invisible.

22
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:57,130
Hmm...

23
00:00:57,213 --> 00:00:58,120
Does this mean this Mr.

24
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:01,017
Joestar is gonna stick
around Morioh for a while?

25
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:01,930
Probably.

26
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:04,090
I see.

27
00:01:04,173 --> 00:01:07,440
Hey, Koichi, do you happen
to like manga? Manga?

28
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:10,605
Yeah, guess I like him
as much as the next guy.

29
00:01:10,780 --> 00:01:12,677
Have you ever heard of Rohan Kishibe?

30
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:14,180
He draws Pink Dark Boy!

31
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:15,757
What kind of question is that?

32
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:18,277
I'm one of the biggest Pink
Dark Boy fans in Japan!

33
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:19,190
No way!

34
00:01:19,273 --> 00:01:20,103
You really like it?

35
00:01:20,186 --> 00:01:21,997
You're talking about the suspense
horror series, aren't you?

36
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:24,257
I never get it mixed
up with anything else!

37
00:01:24,340 --> 00:01:26,037
It can get pretty gross sometimes,

38
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:29,177
but it's worth it for the horror
aesthetic and complex characters.

39
00:01:29,260 --> 00:01:30,378
I completely agree!

40
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:32,617
By the way, here's a little secret.

41
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:35,477
Rohan Kishibe actually
lives right here in Morioh.

42
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:36,390
What?

43
00:01:36,473 --> 00:01:37,337
Did I hear you right?

44
00:01:37,420 --> 00:01:38,797
He lives here in Morioh?

45
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:41,117
It's almost too good to
be true, are you sure?

46
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:43,117
I know, I couldn't believe it either!

47
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:46,337
I heard some realtors talking about
it while I was at the comic store.

48
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:49,277
It's mind-boggling news,
but it's absolutely true!

49
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:50,190
Yeah!

50
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:51,760
I just had a great idea!

51
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:53,237
Let's get some autographs!

52
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:54,340
You know it!

53
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:55,559
Just lead the way!

54
00:01:58,060 --> 00:02:00,920
We really get each
other, huh? You think so?

55
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:04,680
Hey, look up there!

56
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:06,597
I think that might be his studio.

57
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:07,562
The light's on!

58
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:08,920
Yeah, you're right.

59
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:11,840
Hey, I wonder if Rohan has any family.

60
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:13,917
From what I hear, he lives alone.

61
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,037
He made his debut four years
ago, back when he was 16.

62
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:17,950
Say what?

63
00:02:18,033 --> 00:02:19,500
He's only 20 years old?

64
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:22,984
That means he was about
my age when he went pro.

65
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:25,997
Snooping around out here
won't do us any good, Koichi.

66
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,797
You're gonna have to ring the doorbell.

67
00:02:27,880 --> 00:02:28,710
Huh?

68
00:02:28,793 --> 00:02:29,697
But why do I have to do it?

69
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:30,780
Isn't it obvious?

70
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:32,409
I have seniority over you.

71
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:35,197
And to be honest, this kind
of stuff makes me nervous.

72
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:37,120
Oh, that's not fair at all.

73
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:02,340
I recognize him!

74
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:03,760
It's Rohan Kishibe!

75
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,471
He looks just like his picture
on the cover of that special

76
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:08,990
New Year's edition!

77
00:03:09,073 --> 00:03:10,780
I mean, Mr. Rohan!

78
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:17,420
And who, pray tell, are you?

79
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:18,900
Why are you here?

80
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:20,700
Some kind of prank? No!

81
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:21,977
We'd never do that!

82
00:03:22,060 --> 00:03:22,890
Honest!

83
00:03:22,973 --> 00:03:24,937
We're students from
Burugahoka High School!

84
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:29,100
Yeah, we're fans of yours,
Sensei! Fans? Of me? Really?

85
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:31,277
My address must have gotten leaked.

86
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:32,397
That's not it at all.

87
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:34,697
I just happened to hear it in passing.

88
00:03:34,780 --> 00:03:36,537
I hope it's not too much trouble, Mr.

89
00:03:36,620 --> 00:03:38,857
Rohan, but could we have
a couple of autographs?

90
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:40,157
It'd really make our day.

91
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:41,580
So you're fans, eh?

92
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:43,870
Tremendous.

93
00:03:43,953 --> 00:03:46,033
We might just be on the same wavelength.

94
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:47,820
Nothing, don't mind me.

95
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:49,037
Please come in.

96
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:53,100
It'd be a pleasure to sign autographs
for two of my biggest fans.

97
00:03:54,460 --> 00:03:55,290
You see?

98
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:56,812
Aren't you glad we came?

99
00:03:57,580 --> 00:03:58,410
I know.

100
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:02,092
How would you like a little
studio tour while you're here?

101
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:04,757
You'd really let us see
where the magic happens?

102
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:08,637
I've already finished today's work,
but if you're still interested then...

103
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:09,550
We are!

104
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:12,360
Pardon the intrusion!

105
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:23,240
Here it is.

106
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:25,420
Oh, amazing!

107
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,840
Whoa, those are four color originals!

108
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:34,470
Oh, stunning!

109
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:36,660
It's even more powerful in person!

110
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:39,220
This is the most magical day ever!

111
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,860
I'm so glad we're here!

112
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:45,457
So I have to know, sensei, how long
have you been working at a Morioh?

113
00:04:45,540 --> 00:04:47,517
I've been living here
for about three months.

114
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:49,360
My family lives in S-City,

115
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:52,892
but when I was a child, we
actually called Mariah our home.

116
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:55,671
Tokyo has its perks, but it's too chaotic.

117
00:04:55,920 --> 00:05:00,360
It has none of Morio's serenity and
isn't at all conducive to creativity.

118
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:02,250
And besides,

119
00:05:02,333 --> 00:05:05,897
today's fax machines and photocopiers
are more advanced than they've ever been.

120
00:05:05,980 --> 00:05:08,745
I can send a complete
manuscript in four hours.

121
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:13,724
No point living in the city now, unless
you care about status and all that drivel.

122
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:16,477
So, uh, what about your
assistants and staff?

123
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:18,880
How do they factor in? They don't.

124
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,680
I work alone. What?

125
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:22,137
There's just no way!

126
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:25,017
You get 19 pages of complex
drawings done in a week!

127
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:26,597
Four days, actually. What?

128
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:28,017
Five if they're in color.

129
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:30,817
On off days, I amuse myself
with travel and such.

130
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:34,897
I'm not much of a people person, which
is why I chose to be a manga artist.

131
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:38,039
An assistant would only be
an unnecessary hindrance.

132
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:39,720
Wow, that's so amazing!

133
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:41,174
You're a total genius!

134
00:05:42,060 --> 00:05:43,320
Please, excuse me.

135
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:44,360
It's a spider!

136
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:50,753
Suburbia never ceases to amaze
with its bugs and spiders.

137
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:55,100
Uh, Mr. Rohan? I see.

138
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:57,520
Hello, Arrhenius ventricosis.

139
00:05:57,880 --> 00:06:00,700
It inhabits homes and
rural areas across Japan.

140
00:06:00,980 --> 00:06:02,568
It's an orb-weaving spider.

141
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:05,426
And a number of them
weave webs day and night.

142
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,240
By the way, you two,

143
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:12,362
do you know what it takes to create
captivating stories for manga?

144
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:18,157
Reality, reality is the driving force
that makes a drawing come totally alive.

145
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:20,497
Its entertainment on the
highest possible level.

146
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:24,000
People assume manga is born
of imagination and fantasy,

147
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:25,657
but they couldn't be more wrong.

148
00:06:25,740 --> 00:06:29,380
A great manga is one that
captures things experienced,

149
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:32,053
seen and felt by flesh and blood beings.

150
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:36,180
Take this exquisite spider for example,

151
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:39,177
something a typical city
dweller would kill in disgust.

152
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:43,297
The way the legs connect to the body
and the positions of its many eyes.

153
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:45,857
Even subtle differences
between the male and female.

154
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:49,837
A manga artist must understand each
of these elements to draw a spider.

155
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:53,117
It's said a spider's silk
solidifies when exposed to air.

156
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:56,376
But have you ever given any
thought to its spinnerets?

157
00:06:56,500 --> 00:07:00,297
And then there's the intricate
arrangement of its internal organs.

158
00:07:00,380 --> 00:07:02,180
How does a spider squirm,

159
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:05,417
especially when it's been sliced
open and awaiting certain death?

160
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:09,720
To depict reality in detail,
one must know such things.

161
00:07:10,420 --> 00:07:12,360
That's barbaric! Silence!

162
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:16,229
How dare an amateur like you
give Rohan Kishibe his opinion!

163
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:19,560
No, I wasn't voicing my
opinion at all! I'm sorry.

164
00:07:21,060 --> 00:07:22,820
Now it's time for a taste.

165
00:07:26,260 --> 00:07:28,580
Holy shit, the stereotype is true!

166
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:31,154
Manga artists really are total weirdos!

167
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:35,480
An excellent expression of agony.

168
00:07:35,980 --> 00:07:40,440
Your vomiting reflex is so raw,
I simply must sketch it. Really?

169
00:07:46,540 --> 00:07:48,364
And now you're just pretending.

170
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:51,357
Let's forget about the sketch.

171
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:52,697
It won't be of any use.

172
00:07:52,780 --> 00:07:53,860
Oh, I'm sorry.

173
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,720
You wanted autographs.

174
00:07:56,860 --> 00:07:59,117
I'll see if I can find
a pen in the kitchen.

175
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:01,360
I'll bring some tea out as well.

176
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:03,109
You don't have to do that!

177
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:07,980
Rohan is great! What a process!

178
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:10,897
Now I know what makes
Pink Dark Boy so amazing!

179
00:08:10,980 --> 00:08:14,333
His need to know every single
detail is on another level!

180
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:15,920
Um, Azamara?

181
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,397
I know we just got here and all, but...

182
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:22,937
Well, uh, don't you think it's
about time for us to get going?

183
00:08:23,020 --> 00:08:23,850
Say what?

184
00:08:23,933 --> 00:08:24,977
You want to go home now?

185
00:08:25,060 --> 00:08:25,890
But why?

186
00:08:25,973 --> 00:08:26,803
Aren't you having fun?

187
00:08:26,886 --> 00:08:29,640
I can't really say why I'm
so nervous all of a sudden.

188
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:32,416
I just have a bad feeling about this.

189
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:35,097
My gut has been known to
be wrong on rare occasions,

190
00:08:35,180 --> 00:08:39,817
but right now it's telling me that there's
something really dangerous about Rohan.

191
00:08:39,900 --> 00:08:40,730
Dangerous?

192
00:08:40,813 --> 00:08:42,031
What do you mean by that?

193
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:43,728
You think he's a stan user?

194
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,920
No, no, it's nothing like that.

195
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:48,040
It's just a weird feeling.

196
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:51,477
Rohan is what those hippie artist
types would call avant-garde,

197
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:52,937
but that doesn't mean
you should immediately

198
00:08:53,020 --> 00:08:55,597
jump to conclusions about
him being a stan user.

199
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:57,917
I already told you, I
don't think he is one.

200
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
I just have a bad feeling, is all.

201
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:01,600
Okay, okay. Let's say Mr.

202
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:03,544
Rohan actually is a stand user.

203
00:09:03,820 --> 00:09:05,977
That'd be amazing for us, don't you think?

204
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:10,057
How awesome would it be to have something
in common with a famous manga artist?

205
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:12,100
But I feel you. So let's leave.

206
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:15,357
If something about him's giving
you the willies, then let's go.

207
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:16,270
Come on.

208
00:09:16,353 --> 00:09:17,660
We can always come back.

209
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:19,500
But one catch!

210
00:09:19,700 --> 00:09:22,617
This thing caught my eye, so
I have to check it out first.

211
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:23,900
A thing? Where?

212
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:24,897
What are you talking about?

213
00:09:24,980 --> 00:09:27,220
Jeez, Koichi, you're so tense.

214
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:30,762
There, it's on top of the
desk next to the phone.

215
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:32,122
Look carefully.

216
00:09:39,660 --> 00:09:41,437
Could that be what I think it is?

217
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:42,857
You better believe it is!

218
00:09:42,940 --> 00:09:44,997
He said he just finished
working on it, remember?

219
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:48,097
I've had my eye on it since we came
in here, and it's the real deal!

220
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:49,777
I never dreamed this would happen.

221
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:52,477
A freshly drawn manuscript
for Pink Dark Boy.

222
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:54,857
Hang on, does this mean
no one else has seen it?

223
00:09:54,940 --> 00:09:57,881
We'll go home right after
I get a glimpse of this.

224
00:09:58,060 --> 00:10:00,413
We have to get Rohan's permission first.

225
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:03,717
You really don't know anything
about manga artists, do you, Koichi?

226
00:10:03,800 --> 00:10:05,597
All of these pre-printed manuscripts are

227
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:08,097
highly confidential in
every sense of the word.

228
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:10,777
There's no way he'd let a couple
of outsiders like us look at

229
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:13,597
a manuscript before the editors
even had a chance to give notes.

230
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:14,760
It's common sense.

231
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:17,197
We'll take a peek, then put it right back.

232
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:19,960
This is a horrible idea. Lighten up.

233
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:22,394
We're not hurting anyone by reading it.

234
00:10:33,920 --> 00:10:35,200
What is this feeling?

235
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:39,397
I know it's a thrilling manga, but
seeing an abusive person like this?

236
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:42,245
is giving me major
goosebumps all over my body!

237
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:44,160
It's so good!

238
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:46,257
Hurry up and turn the page, Hazamada!

239
00:10:46,340 --> 00:10:47,877
I have to know what comes next!

240
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:49,254
I'm getting emotional!

241
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:50,560
What do you know?

242
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:54,497
It appears my manuscript's
compatible with you two after all.

243
00:10:54,580 --> 00:10:55,462
How auspicious.

244
00:10:55,820 --> 00:10:57,697
I had a hunch you might read it.

245
00:10:57,780 --> 00:10:58,920
Good work, boys.

246
00:10:59,100 --> 00:11:03,218
The two of you are compatible
first-time readers of my new manuscript.

247
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:06,140
As I'm not I?

248
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:07,497
What's the matter?

249
00:11:07,580 --> 00:11:11,051
You will now experience my
glorious ability, Heaven's Door.

250
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:13,200
It's a gateway to your very souls.

251
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:14,760
What do you mean?

252
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:16,020
What is going on?

253
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:17,767
Why does my hand feel weird?

254
00:11:21,860 --> 00:11:22,690
What the?

255
00:11:22,820 --> 00:11:25,560
Koichi, what the hell is happening to you?

256
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:40,197
Many things are recorded in the human
body over the course of one's life.

257
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:42,557
Every single thing from
the moment you were born.

258
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:46,228
To peruse your records I shall
transform you both into books.

259
00:11:46,620 --> 00:11:49,738
Magnificent books that
chronicle your life's stories.

260
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:51,510
Not me!

261
00:11:51,593 --> 00:11:52,620
Somebody else!

262
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:55,000
I believe you read my manga as well.

263
00:11:58,300 --> 00:11:59,740
It's happening to me!

264
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:04,162
My ability won't physically harm
you, so there's no need to worry.

265
00:12:04,260 --> 00:12:06,917
What the hell do you
even want from us anyway?

266
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:10,657
In manga, the creator's sense of
reality is critical, remember?

267
00:12:10,740 --> 00:12:11,957
We went over that.

268
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:16,057
So now, I will read all about your
lives and experiences thus far,

269
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:19,817
and these pages will fill my
consciousness with realistic ideas.

270
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:21,841
More effective than an interview,

271
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:25,277
you will tell me everything you've
lived through with 100 % accuracy,

272
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:28,260
as if I had been there
to experience it myself!

273
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:33,640
Koichi Hirose, born March
28, 1984, at 6.27 a .m.

274
00:12:33,840 --> 00:12:36,920
You were delivered at Red
Cross Hospital in S-City.

275
00:12:37,620 --> 00:12:41,880
A preemie of 2,325 grams, you
spent a week in an incubator.

276
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:45,100
A family of four and an
older sister named Ayana.

277
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:46,200
Yes, I see.

278
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:50,697
In grade school and middle school,
you led a relatively ordinary life.

279
00:12:50,780 --> 00:12:53,760
You also happened to be a
remarkably genuine soul.

280
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:55,440
An admirable quality.

281
00:12:58,220 --> 00:12:59,440
What is this?

282
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:03,457
So then you're hiding a secret
ability, are you? Reverb, huh?

283
00:13:03,540 --> 00:13:06,377
And it seems that there
are other individuals

284
00:13:06,460 --> 00:13:08,977
in the world with these
fantastical abilities.

285
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:10,295
You have powers, too?

286
00:13:14,380 --> 00:13:16,780
Stand users, huh? Astounding!

287
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:20,885
Everything in here dated after
April 1999 is just extraordinary!

288
00:13:21,180 --> 00:13:23,480
An explosion of wondrous experiences!

289
00:13:23,980 --> 00:13:26,520
Josuke Higashikata, Jotaro Kujo,

290
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:30,520
Yukako Yamagishi, Okuyasu
Nijimura, Tamami Kobayashi!

291
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:32,217
Oh, it's unbelievable!

292
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:34,600
Incredible and utterly captivating.

293
00:13:34,780 --> 00:13:36,545
In these pages, Koichi Hirose,

294
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:39,936
I've just uncovered the
mother load of manga material.

295
00:13:41,580 --> 00:13:48,560
Shining Diamond, Star Platinum, The
Hand, Love Deluxe, et Star, et Star.

296
00:13:49,140 --> 00:13:50,728
What are you talking about?

297
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:53,477
What the heck are you
planning to do to us now?

298
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:55,325
You mean it isn't obvious yet?

299
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:58,820
I'm going to use your memories
to write my manga. River!

300
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:06,337
I'm only going to ask you nicely once
to stop attacking us with your stand,

301
00:14:06,420 --> 00:14:07,880
if you persist.

302
00:14:08,260 --> 00:14:09,820
Hmm, what will you do?

303
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:13,280
Strike me with reverb act two
sound attack? Just try it.

304
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:14,940
Don't test me.

305
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:18,137
If you don't release me from your
stand right now, I won't hold back.

306
00:14:18,220 --> 00:14:19,577
This is your last chance.

307
00:14:19,660 --> 00:14:20,520
Yes, I know.

308
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:24,257
There's actually a section devoted
to that written on page 11.

309
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:27,217
You've always been far more
timid than most others,

310
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:29,657
and many tend to blatantly disrespect you.

311
00:14:29,740 --> 00:14:34,034
But when push comes to shove, you find
the courage to conquer your fears.

312
00:14:34,360 --> 00:14:35,190
Remarkable.

313
00:14:35,273 --> 00:14:36,340
I like you already.

314
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:40,617
And as for my readers, they'll feel
the same once they get to know you.

315
00:14:40,700 --> 00:14:42,197
I'm not bluffing, you hear me?

316
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:43,617
I'll attack if I have to.

317
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:46,237
You really don't know
when to shut up, do you?

318
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:47,620
Try it if you dare!

319
00:14:48,080 --> 00:14:49,400
Reverb, act two, go!

320
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:57,440
I don't get it!

321
00:14:57,560 --> 00:14:58,795
How'd my attack miss?

322
00:14:58,920 --> 00:15:00,657
You honestly missed at that range?

323
00:15:00,740 --> 00:15:02,937
I thought you let it go wide on purpose!

324
00:15:03,020 --> 00:15:05,844
I hate to break it to
you, but your aim is shit!

325
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:08,300
I won't miss this time!

326
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:11,577
Where are you attacking?

327
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:12,897
That wasn't even close!

328
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:14,717
Unfortunately for you, Koichi,

329
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:18,388
I took the liberty of placing
a little safety lock on Reverb.

330
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:24,017
You can attack me to your heart's content,
but you're no longer able to land a blow.

331
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:25,000
Safety lock?

332
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:30,030
Take a look.

333
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,965
It's in the margin on page 11.

334
00:15:32,580 --> 00:15:35,417
I added that new rule as a
little bit of a safety measure,

335
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:37,441
just in case you used your stand.

336
00:15:46,660 --> 00:15:47,580
Do you see?

337
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:50,329
This is the awesome
power of Heaven's Door.

338
00:15:50,420 --> 00:15:51,250
Through it,

339
00:15:51,333 --> 00:15:53,097
I can use words and
pictures to read people's

340
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:55,592
experiences or create brand new memories.

341
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:58,417
It doesn't matter what sort of
tricks you have up your sleeve.

342
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:01,597
You'll never be able to do me
harm as long as I have this power.

343
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:02,510
Shit!

344
00:16:02,593 --> 00:16:03,423
What do I do now?

345
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:10,080
Chin up, Koichi.

346
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:12,397
That's all the tampering I intend to do.

347
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:14,417
If I meddled with your pages any further,

348
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:16,497
your precious life would
lose all authenticity?

349
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:19,462
and you'd no longer be of
any benefit to my work.

350
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:20,910
All right.

351
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:23,477
Now let's have a look
at your pages, Hazamada.

352
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:25,977
You're a genius in every
sense of the word, sir!

353
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:27,760
I respect you so much!

354
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:30,740
I suppose we'll see about that. Now then,

355
00:16:31,140 --> 00:16:34,957
you sometimes find a sense of comfort
in picking on creatures weaker than you?

356
00:16:35,040 --> 00:16:37,275
like helpless kittens and small birds.

357
00:16:37,840 --> 00:16:41,369
You want to have your way with
Junko, a junior from Class E,

358
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:43,500
but are too cowardly to act on it.

359
00:16:43,900 --> 00:16:47,937
Your testicles often grow sweaty, and
when you adjust them during class,

360
00:16:48,020 --> 00:16:49,557
nothing thrills you more than the thought?

361
00:16:49,640 --> 00:16:51,228
that someone might see you.

362
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,720
You're a disgusting troll.

363
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:57,765
Including someone like you in my
manga would drive readers away.

364
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,040
You're useless.

365
00:17:01,800 --> 00:17:03,480
What am I gonna do now?

366
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:05,400
I'm hopeless. Why?

367
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:08,580
Why are you doing this?

368
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:11,417
You don't need any of my
experiences to create stories.

369
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:14,197
You're a spectacular manga
artist all on your own.

370
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:16,237
Every reader in the world knows that.

371
00:17:16,320 --> 00:17:19,317
Also, you're only 20 years old
and live in this amazing house.

372
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:22,597
Think of how blessed you are
compared with most people your age.

373
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:25,974
So why do you need my memories
when you're already grey?

374
00:17:27,240 --> 00:17:28,900
How stupid can you be?

375
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:33,708
Do you think that I, Rohan Kishibe, draw
manga to gather money and admiration?

376
00:17:34,180 --> 00:17:37,592
I draw manga so that people
around the world will read it.

377
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:40,297
My only objective is for
people to read my work.

378
00:17:40,380 --> 00:17:42,377
I know it's a single simple reason.

379
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:44,284
Even so, it's all I care about.

380
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:46,677
People want honesty
when they read my work,

381
00:17:46,760 --> 00:17:49,584
so I search for inspirational
realism every day.

382
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:53,977
And truth be told, I absolutely love
the feeling of finishing a manuscript.

383
00:17:54,060 --> 00:17:57,377
Everyone feels good after finishing
a project they've worked hard on,

384
00:17:57,460 --> 00:18:00,197
but that gratification is
fleeting and immaterial.

385
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:02,737
After the initial rush
of euphoria is gone,

386
00:18:02,820 --> 00:18:05,777
I begin to think no one will
read the manga I slaved over?

387
00:18:05,860 --> 00:18:08,797
and my deep-seated
insecurities begin to flare up.

388
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:11,527
What if all my readers
are gone by next week?

389
00:18:11,660 --> 00:18:14,437
What if I don't know what
to draw for the next issue?

390
00:18:14,520 --> 00:18:16,579
What if I lose the ability to draw?

391
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:18,701
What if my motivation disappears?

392
00:18:20,520 --> 00:18:23,897
These are the recurring thoughts
that have tormented me over and over?

393
00:18:23,980 --> 00:18:26,180
since I was a 16-year-old novice.

394
00:18:26,300 --> 00:18:30,537
Until three months ago when a mysterious
stranger shot me to the core with an arrow?

395
00:18:30,620 --> 00:18:33,091
and I gained the ability of Heaven's Door.

396
00:18:33,180 --> 00:18:34,709
That was Keicho Nichimura.

397
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:37,391
Yes, I saw his name written on your pages.

398
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:40,657
You two have no idea what it's like
to find the perfect inspiration?

399
00:18:40,740 --> 00:18:42,505
for your ultimate masterpiece.

400
00:18:42,820 --> 00:18:44,780
But I found it at last.

401
00:18:45,180 --> 00:18:46,177
There's nothing better.

402
00:18:46,260 --> 00:18:51,220
Koichi, I'm taking your reality and
using it as a muse for my new stories!

403
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:07,620
See, Koichi, I told you Mr.

404
00:19:07,740 --> 00:19:09,217
Rohan was a super nice guy.

405
00:19:09,300 --> 00:19:11,377
Aren't you glad we decided
to pay him a visit?

406
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:13,284
Definitely, I had a ton of fun.

407
00:19:13,520 --> 00:19:15,757
Not only did he give us
these great autographs,

408
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:18,217
He was even kind enough to
serve us tea and cookies.

409
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:19,130
Mm-hmm.

410
00:19:19,213 --> 00:19:20,357
I want to go back as soon as we can.

411
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:21,270
Me too.

412
00:19:21,353 --> 00:19:22,380
Today kicked ass!

413
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:23,697
Well, I'm headed this way.

414
00:19:23,780 --> 00:19:24,610
See you later.

415
00:19:26,220 --> 00:19:28,808
I'm still surprised he
was such a great guy.

416
00:19:39,080 --> 00:19:42,080
You'll never speak of what
happened, right, Koichi?

417
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:47,370
What the?

418
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:49,896
How the heck did I lose 20 kilograms?

419
00:19:52,760 --> 00:19:53,701
That's so weird.

420
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:55,212
I look exactly the same.

421
00:19:56,920 --> 00:20:00,160
Yep, it reads 5 kilograms,
so the scale's not broken.

422
00:20:03,780 --> 00:20:05,480
This doesn't make any sense!

423
00:20:05,980 --> 00:20:08,737
Wait, this must be the work
of an enemy stand user!

424
00:20:08,820 --> 00:20:12,517
There's no other way I could
possibly lose 20 kilograms this fast!

425
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:14,000
But who's the user?

426
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:16,518
I have to talk to Josuke about the -

427
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:17,850
Huh?

428
00:20:19,560 --> 00:20:22,460
Hey, Ko, what are you
doing over there? Huh?

429
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:24,270
Me?

430
00:20:24,760 --> 00:20:26,377
Uh, well, I...

431
00:20:26,460 --> 00:20:28,080
Huh, what was it?

432
00:20:28,380 --> 00:20:30,697
What the hell are you
talking about, you weirdo?

433
00:20:30,780 --> 00:20:31,839
Hey, what's wrong?

434
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:33,337
Oh, it's just my brother.

435
00:20:33,420 --> 00:20:36,417
For some reason, he's wandering
around the house in his goofy boxers.

436
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:37,330
What was it?

437
00:20:37,413 --> 00:20:41,626
I could have sworn I was thinking about
something really important a second ago.

438
00:20:45,120 --> 00:20:49,649
Well, if I managed to forget so easily,
it couldn't have been that important.

439
00:20:53,860 --> 00:20:54,840
Oh, man.

440
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:59,800
Why do my shoes and bag feel
heavier than usual today? Hold on.

441
00:21:01,980 --> 00:21:02,940
This house!

442
00:21:03,780 --> 00:21:04,840
How strange.

443
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:09,327
Somehow, I ended up walking all
the way back to Rohan's house.

444
00:21:10,760 --> 00:21:11,940
The door's open.

445
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:16,417
I'd like to drop in and thank him for
being such a great host yesterday.

446
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:18,147
But I'll be late for school.

447
00:21:18,420 --> 00:21:19,960
I probably shouldn't.

448
00:21:20,860 --> 00:21:23,448
Being an artist, he's
probably still asleep.

449
00:21:23,980 --> 00:21:25,760
It'd be rude to just barge in.

450
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:28,160
I really shouldn't.

451
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:37,940
You saw that, right, Okuyasu?

452
00:21:39,740 --> 00:21:40,570
Yeah...

453
00:21:40,653 --> 00:21:41,500
Spying feels wrong,

454
00:21:41,660 --> 00:21:45,157
but it's out of character for Koichi
to act so weird and ditch school.

455
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:46,757
What the hell is he doing?

456
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:49,097
Well, I want to know who
in the world lives here.

457
00:21:49,180 --> 00:21:52,827
I mean, there's no way he's
meeting up with some chick, right?

458
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:07,910
Rohan,

459
00:22:07,993 --> 00:22:11,717
he's working with such a chilling
expression and for some reason I

460
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:14,917
can't shake the feeling that being
in this house is actually terrifying?

461
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:19,277
Why you finally made it?

462
00:22:19,360 --> 00:22:20,477
It's good to see you!

463
00:22:20,560 --> 00:22:22,340
Right on time for our session.

464
00:23:04,953 --> 00:23:06,757
We'll

465
00:23:06,840 --> 00:23:13,840
be

466
00:23:23,520 --> 00:23:24,350
right back.
